{"name":"Black Cat","hex":"#2e2f31","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Black Cat","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["someone connected with Sunderland Football Club, as a fan, player, coach etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Black_Cat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black cat","blocks":[{"text":"A black cat is a domestic cat with black fur. They may be a specific breed, or a common domestic cat of no particular breed. Most black cats have golden irises due to their high melanin pigment content. Black cats are the subject of mythology, legend, and superstition. They are often associated with witches and good or bad luck in European folklore."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Blackcat-Lilith.jpg/330px-Blackcat-Lilith.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_cat"},{"title":"Black Cat (Harvey Comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Black Cat is a comic book adventure heroine published by Harvey Comics from 1941 to 1951. Harvey also published reprints of the character in both the mid-1950s and the early 1960s. The character's creation is claimed by the Harvey family to have originated with publisher Alfred Harvey, but there is no corroborating evidence for this. The Black Cat debuted in Pocket Comics #1."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/BlackCatNo1A.png/330px-BlackCatNo1A.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Cat_(Harvey_Comics)"},{"title":"Black Cat (Marvel Comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Black Cat is a character appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. Created by Marv Wolfman and Dave Cockrum, the character first appeared in The Amazing Spider-Man #194 in July 1979 as an adversary of the superhero Spider-Man, although she later becomes his on-off love interest and ally."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ee/Black_Cat_%28Felicia_Hardy%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Cat_(Marvel_Comics)"},{"title":"Cat","blocks":[{"text":"The cat, also called domestic cat and house cat, is a small domesticated carnivorous mammal. It is a member of Felidae, the family of mammals in the order Carnivora also colloquially referred to as cats. An obligate carnivore requiring a predominantly meat-based diet, it has retractable claws adapted to killing small prey species such as mice and rats. It has a strong, flexible body, quick reflexes, and sharp teeth, and its night vision and sense of smell are well developed. It is a social species, but a solitary hunter and a crepuscular predator.\nCat communication includes meowing, purring, trilling, hissing, growling, grunting, body language, and scent marking. It can hear sounds too faint or too high in frequency for human ears, such as those made by small mammals. It secretes and perceives pheromones. Cat intelligence is evident in its ability to adapt, learn through observation, and solve problems. The domestic cat is the only domesticated species of the family Felidae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Siam_lilacpoint.jpg/330px-Siam_lilacpoint.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cat"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Mauegytiensmoke.jpg/250px-Mauegytiensmoke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Mauegytiensmoke.jpg/330px-Mauegytiensmoke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Mauegytiensmoke.jpg/250px-Mauegytiensmoke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMauegytiensmoke.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Kot_czarny.jpg/250px-Kot_czarny.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Kot_czarny.jpg/330px-Kot_czarny.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Kot_czarny.jpg/250px-Kot_czarny.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKot_czarny.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Black_pussy_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Black_pussy_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Black_pussy_-_panoramio.jpg/1280px-Black_pussy_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Black_pussy_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Black_pussy_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Some cultures are superstitious about black cats, ascribing either good or bad luck to them.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlack_pussy_-_panoramio.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Casting_black_cats_in_1961.jpg/500px-Casting_black_cats_in_1961.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Casting_black_cats_in_1961.jpg/1280px-Casting_black_cats_in_1961.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Casting_black_cats_in_1961.jpg/500px-Casting_black_cats_in_1961.jpg?utm_sourc